    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d113">

                <pb facs="0205" n="939" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg939"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Baron
                            Fava.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-03-14"><hi rendition="#italic">March 14,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Baron</hi>: In connection with my note to you
                    of yesterday concerning the reported violence in Colorado, I take pleasure in
                    herewith transmitting for your further information a copy of my telegram to his
                    excellency the governor of that State, and copies of Governor McIntire’s two
                    replies of yesterday and to-day. The first reached me late last night and the
                    second early this morning.</p>
                <p>Very truly, yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>





